1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,543
Visualize History shows what a Set said on every past day.

2
00:00:03,593 --> 00:00:05,877
Open a scan, and press the clock.

3
00:00:17,568 --> 00:00:20,471
The price is drawn with coloured bands behind it.

4
00:00:20,521 --> 00:00:22,847
Green is Yes. Amber is Unknown.

5
00:00:22,897 --> 00:00:24,584
No is left clear.

6
00:00:25,023 --> 00:00:28,993
Underneath, every other asset in the scan gets a small chart of its own,

7
00:00:29,013 --> 00:00:30,422
with the same bands.

8
00:00:30,472 --> 00:00:32,649
So you can compare them at a glance.

9
00:00:33,088 --> 00:00:36,268
Tap a small chart, and that asset moves to the top.

10
00:00:46,656 --> 00:00:50,497
Choose how far back to look: one year, three, ten, or everything.

11
00:00:50,547 --> 00:00:54,090
Older years load in the background, marked with an hourglass.

12
00:01:13,556 --> 00:01:18,571
Open on the main price chart takes the asset and its bands to your dashboard chart.

13
00:01:19,004 --> 00:01:21,459
The bands show when the conditions were met.

14
00:01:21,509 --> 00:01:23,686
They don't say what happened next.

15
00:01:23,736 --> 00:01:26,041
That is the job of the next video.
